  "worked_solution": "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B+1 & =4 \\\\ A+B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=-2A{e}^{-2x}+2B{e}^{2x}-2,\n$$\n\nand then we substitute ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=0$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2A+2B-2 & =0 \\\\ A-B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=3 \\\\ A-B=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=1,B=2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-2x}+2{e}^{2x}-2x+1.\n$$",
